  "body": "What happens: the posed sweep of the fixture laws (c2)/(d2) (`crates/sim/src/verify/posed_steel.rs`) places each band of a leaning stack as a capsule, and a capsule's caps reach one whole band radius past each end of the band, along the axis. So a holder standing just over a clamp is clear upright (and within `UPRIGHT_TILT_RAD`, #938) but convicted `FixtureHit` at any tilt above it: the same cliff #1303 removed from the column laws, from a different enclosure.\n\nExpected: the posed sweep encloses a band as the cylinder it is (flat ends: the rim reaches R·sin θ past the end plane, not R), so the fixture verdict changes continuously with the tilt.\n\nEvidence: `crates/sim/tests/tilt_tolerance.rs::the_fixture_band_law_reads_noise_as_upright_and_a_real_tilt_as_tilted` - an r 15 holder whose bottom stands 0.5 mm over a clamp is clear upright and convicted at 1.01e-9 rad. After #1303 the column half of the law (`stack_span::band_struck`) is clear there (unit test `verify::tilt_band::consumers::the_fixture_band_column_dips_by_the_rim_and_strikes_only_when_it_reaches`: clear up to 1.7 degrees, struck from 2.1); the conviction comes from `posed_steel::posed_hits` alone. The verdict is conservative (a false collision, never a missed one).\n\nNotes for whoever takes it: this needs a cylinder-box (or cylinder-AABB swept) distance in place of the segment-box distance plus radius; the swing/travel growth of the capsule radius must still enclose the swept volume. Check the mesh twin (`mesh_posed.rs`) and the part-solid probe atoms for the same end-cap reading while there.\n\nDone means: a holder 0.5 mm over a clamp is not convicted at 0.01 degrees and is convicted once its rim really reaches the clamp, pinned both ways, with a property check that the enclosure still contains sampled points of the tilted band over the interval's swing.\n\nFound while fixing #1303 (follow-up of #938).\n",
